; Article-stripping objects (checks 109-110, owner ruling 2026-08-05).
; Each text is chosen for what it does to the article matcher:
;   10 "some silver keys" - the "some " case (nothing else in this
;      fixture starts with an article other than "a "/"an ").
;   11 "rusty anvil"      - a first word that is NOT an article, which
;      must SURVIVE substitution. This is the owner's "rusty sword"
;      case; the noun is ANVIL rather than SWORD only so it cannot
;      reach checks 87-96.
;   12 "somersault rope"  - matches "some" for four characters and then
;      diverges on the fifth, where the space should be. The deepest
;      case the no-peek matcher has to unwind, and the one a
;      buffer-and-replay implementation gets wrong (it prints "rope",
;      or "somersault rope" out of order). "some" and "the" share one
;      pattern walker in the interpreter, so this covers the "theatre"
;      shape on the "the" arm too - one fixture, both arms.
;   13 "the iron gate"    - the "the " case (owner ruling 2026-08-05 on
;      a 323-text corpus survey: 27 object texts start with "the", 19
;      of them in MYST_EN). TWO words survive the strip on purpose - a
;      matcher that ate one word too many would print "gate" and a
;      one-word expectation could not tell that apart.
/10 "some silver keys"
/11 "rusty anvil"
/12 "somersault rope"
/13 "the iron gate"
