/OBJ
; Columns: number, starts at, weight, then c(ontainer) w(earable),
; then the 16 extended attribute columns, then noun/adjective. The
; DAAD template's own column ruler for those 16 reads
;     5 4 3 2 1 0 9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0
; i.e. attribute 15 LEFTMOST down to attribute 0 RIGHTMOST, across
; the whole word (NOT per-byte). Verified against DRC 0.40/0.35
; output, which is what SP16 check 47 pins:
;     last column Y  -> extra-attribute bytes 01 00 (attribute 0)
;     8th column Y   -> extra-attribute bytes 00 01 (attribute 8)
; The DDB word is LITTLE ENDIAN (drb.php generateObjectExtraAttr),
; so the first byte is attributes 0-7 and belongs in flag 59 (40 for
; the second referenced object), the second is 8-15 and belongs in
; flag 58 (39). Lamp carries attribute 0 and box/coin attribute 8 so
; that check 47 can tell the two apart in both directions.
/0    CARRIED     1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ Y   LAMP _
/1    0           2   Y _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ Y _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   BOX  _
/2    NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ Y _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   COIN _
/3    0           1   _ Y  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   HAT  _
; SP16 Task 3 (checks 87-96). All six start NOT_CREATED on purpose, so
; no earlier check can see them: the DOALL-over-location-0 counters
; (34, 49, 86) and the LISTAT of location 0 (36) skip them, and none of
; them sits on a location number that WEIGH 1 (check 27) would read as
; "inside object 1". They are CREATEd by the checks that need them.
; 4/5 share a noun and BOTH carry an adjective - the D1 partial-match
; case. 6/7 share a noun with the ADJECTIVED one first, so a resolver
; that returns the first partial instead of holding out for the full
; match picks the wrong one. 8 is the zero-weight "magic bag" (B29)
; and 9 is what goes inside it.
/4    NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   SWORD RUSTY
/5    NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   SWORD SHINY
/6    NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   ROBE  SMALL
/7    NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   ROBE  _
/8    NOT_CREATED 0   Y _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   BAG   _
/9    NOT_CREATED 5   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   GEM   _
; Article-stripping objects (checks 109-110). NOT_CREATED like 4-9, so
; no earlier check can see them; 109/110 place them themselves.
/10   NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   KEYS  _
/11   NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   ANVIL _
/12   NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   ROPE  _
/13   NOT_CREATED 1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   GATE  _
