; 04 INVERTED 2026-08-04 (owner ruling). This check used to read
; "NOTZERO 37" and pin the pre-initialisation of flag 37 to 4 and flag
; 52 to 10 at eng_init_game. Neither reference does that - msx2daad
; memsets every flag to zero and writes fMaxCarr/fStrength only in
; do_ABILITY, and jDAAD's resetFlags has no exceptions either - so the
; pre-init was removed and this check now pins its ABSENCE.
;
; It must stay HERE, at the top of the table: the suite's own first
; ABILITY is check 33 (line ~271 below) and several later checks LET 37
; and 52 directly, so anything further down would read those instead.
; Safe against a re-run because it cannot happen - PRO 1's last entry
; chains PRO 5..14 into the E03 process-stack overflow, and err_raise
; is terminal (src/errors.asm "both funnels are terminal and never
; return"), so this table executes exactly once per session. Checks
; 01-03 above touch flag 100 only.
;
; The screen label carries its meaning because "04 OK" alone would now
; mean the opposite of what it meant before; it keeps "04 OK" as its
; leading token so the eye-scan and the 114-line count are unchanged.
> _ _   ZERO 37
        ZERO 52
        MES "04 OK 37/52 ZERO#n"
        SKIP 1
> _ _   MES "04 F#n"
